Year = {1997},
Volume = {96},
Number = {1-3},
Pages = {11-28},
Month = {MAR 1},
Abstract = {Following a comparison of current alternative approaches for modelling
   and prediction of algal blooms, artificial neural networks are
   introduced and applied as a new, promising model type. The neural
   network applications were developed and validated by limnological
   time-series from four different freshwater systems, The water-specific
   time-series comprised cell numbers or biomass of the ten dominating
   algae species as observed over up to twelve years and the measured
   environmental driving variables. The resulting predictions on
   succession, timing and magnitudes of algal species indicate that
   artificial neural networks can fit the complexity and nonlinearity of
   ecological phenomena apparently to a high degree. (C) 1997 Elsevier
   Science B.V.},
