Month = {MAR},
Abstract = {Mating preferences for specific traits increase the fertility, fecundity
   or offspring fitness of choosy individuals. However, current fitness
   benefits offer an incomplete account of the relative influence of
   different signals on mate choice. The history of selection on sensory
   systems in a broader ecological context can provide many missing
