   1993},
Abstract = {Remote sensing has considerable potential for vegetation mapping. The
   model of vegetation distribution represented in an image classification,
   however, may not always be appropriate as the algorithms typically used
   give a `hard' class allocation. Here the output of three classification
   techniques, a maximum likelihood, artificial neural network and fuzzy
   sets classification, are softened and shown to be able to reflect the
   class composition of image pixels and so be able to provide a better
   representation of some vegetation from remotely sensed imagery.},
